  "// archetypes": "Pointwise operations are almost never run alone -- they sit on the output of a convolution, a projection or an attention score matrix, and inherit its shape. The archetypes are those tensors, plus the flat case where only the element count matters.",
  "// neighbourhood": "D3 mirrors D2 at ratio 1 so the square cases stay square; a scaled D3 would turn an attention score tensor into a rectangle no attention produces.",
  "// elements": "Two inputs and one output. Every declared mode -- ADD, MUL, SUB, DIV, MAX_OP, MIN_OP -- is binary, so the traffic does not vary with it. Element count across every tensor the operation touches, inputs and outputs. Dtype-free on purpose: bytes is elements times the dtype width, and the width table belongs to the tool rather than repeated as a nested dtype lookup in seven declarations. gbs = bytes / measured time, which is the metric that ranks a memory-bound kernel where tflops cannot.",
